# Generated from: specs/195-move-exact-head-delivery-into-a-controller-with-on-demand-remediation/requirements.md
Feature: Move exact-head delivery into a controller with on-demand remediation
  As a deliver worker
  I want version bump, PR create/resume, CI/thread classification, exact-head merge, and merge+close proof to run in code
  So that a model is prompted only when a bot thread or CI failure needs a code change

  # --- Happy Path ---

  @SCN001
  Scenario: green delivery completes without remediation prompt weight
    Given issue N has an approved spec, current verification, and a green exact-branch PR
    When the sibling deliver worker runs node scripts/sdlc-deliver.mjs --issue N
    Then the controller preserves version synchronization, push, PR create or resume, and readiness classification
    And it merges with --match-head-commit for the observed head
    And it writes a passed deliver handoff only after PR MERGED at that head and issue CLOSED
    And it deletes the local issue branch only after that proof
    And no Address PR Comments workflow is inlined

  @SCN002
  Scenario: clear automated finding requests same-worker remediation
    Given the PR has an unresolved automated-review thread or failing in-scope check requiring an edit
    When the controller classifies delivery state
    Then it prints one NMG_SDLC_REMEDIATION JSON packet and exits 3
    And the packet identifies the issue, PR, head SHA, checks, thread context, and handoff path
    And the same deliver worker applies a clear local safe fix, verifies, pushes without force, and reruns the controller
    And no nested OMP worker is started and no prompt is resent

  # --- Alternative Paths ---

  @SCN003
  Scenario: existing delivery PR resumes idempotently
    Given the exact branch already has an open delivery PR with synchronized version artifacts
    When the controller runs again
    Then it does not increment the version a second time
    And it re-fetches the current head, checks, reviews, and threads
    And it continues from current classified state

  @SCN004
  Scenario: pending checks stop after a bounded wait
    Given required checks or automated review remain pending without an actionable failure
    When one hour elapses from the initial observation
    Then observations have been at least 30 seconds apart
    And the controller writes a failed delivery_pending intervention handoff
    And it does not merge

  # --- Error Handling ---

  @SCN005
  Scenario: human or ambiguous review prevents merge
    Given an unresolved human thread, CHANGES_REQUESTED review, or ambiguous bot request
    When delivery classifies the review
    Then the controller writes a failed human_review intervention handoff
    And an ambiguous remediation is reported through --remediation-result human_review
    And the thread is not resolved and the PR is not merged

  @SCN006
  Scenario: breaking work requires approved major bump
    Given issue title or body contains BREAKING
    And approved requirements and design omit Version bump major
    When the controller evaluates versioning
    Then it writes a failed major_bump_required intervention handoff
    And it does not change version files or create a PR

  @SCN007
  Scenario: merge proof failure cannot report success
    Given the controller attempted exact-head merge at head H without branch deletion
    When the refreshed PR is not MERGED at H or the issue is not CLOSED
    Then it writes a failed merge_failed intervention handoff
    And it deletes neither the local nor remote issue branch

  @SCN008
  Scenario: invalid delivery CLI has no side effects
    Given the CLI lacks a valid --issue N or contains unknown arguments
    When scripts/sdlc-deliver.mjs runs
    Then it prints the usage contract and exits 2
    And it writes no handoff and invokes neither gh nor git

  @SCN009
  Scenario: verification proves two real smoke issue lifecycles
    Given the issue 195 implementation is ready for verification
    When the verification worker runs two distinct issues against the GitHub repository Nunley-Media-Group/nmg-sdlc-smoke-20260820001416
    Then each issue creates a pull request that merges at its observed exact head and closes the issue
    And the verification handoff preserves fresh issue URLs, pull request URLs, head SHAs, merged states, and closed states
    And unit tests or fixture exercises cannot substitute for this evidence
    And unavailable GitHub, repository, Herdr, merge, or closure prerequisites fail verification
